Fix stray brace that broke the Edge Function bundle

My earlier line surgery, moving a misplaced block out of performUndo, left a
duplicate closer behind: }) followed by a stray } at the end of the
CONTENT_WRITE_TOOLS declaration. Deno's type checker accepted the file, but the
Supabase bundler rejected it, so the deploy failed with:

  The module's source code could not be parsed: Expression expected at
  .../index.ts:2037:1

Removed the stray brace and confirmed all four function modules check cleanly.

Add scripts/check-edge-functions.mjs, wired to 
pm run deploy:agent, so this
class of failure cannot reach a deploy again. It:
  - locates Deno automatically, including the WinGet package directory, since
    deno is not reliably on PATH in a fresh shell
  - checks every module the function bundles, not just index.ts
  - prints only the diagnostics, and refuses to deploy on any error
  - warns and continues when Deno is absent, so it never blocks a deploy for
    someone who lacks it

Also adds npm run sync:theme for the theme token sync.
